desc:ReaProof Serialize BROKEN (trusts the stream)
// Deliberately-broken variant for catalog item 4: the restore path reads a
// COUNT from the stream and then loop-reads that many values straight into
// slider1 without checking file_avail() - the classic silent-truncation bug.
// With a payload cut mid-stream it half-restores: the first value lands, the
// missing ones read as 0, and the accumulated slider is garbage instead of
// the declared default. The battery truncates the payload and demands
// defaults; this subject must turn that check RED.

slider1:0<-24,24,0.01>Gain (dB)

in_pin:left input
in_pin:right input
out_pin:left output
out_pin:right output

@init
n = 2; a = 11; b = 22;

@slider
gain = 10^(slider1/20);

@sample
spl0 *= gain;
spl1 *= gain;

@serialize
file_avail(0) >= 0 ? (
  file_var(0, rn);
  ri = 0;
  while (ri < rn) (
    file_var(0, rv);
    slider1 += rv;      // half-read applied as if valid
    ri += 1;
  );
) : (
  file_var(0, n);
  file_var(0, a);
  file_var(0, b);
);
